    rdf:value """off. But I hope she will be kinder to him than that.
Mr. and Mrs. Nowers spent ten days here very pleasantly. Blair Fairchild, who is a nice boy, was also here. One evening we spoke of insanity, and he turned pale and could not eat. Afterwards he told Bernhard he had lost his mind several times, and lived in dread of it. Poor boy! Poor boy! His form of insanity is falling into a belief in the Jesuits (a nurse made him secretly a Catholic when he was a small child), and once during """^^xsd:string ;
